1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,450
The $50 Million 'Gift' of 1942

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:09,360
On the 25th of June 1942, four
months into the Japanese Occupation,

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,786
the 72-year-old Lim Boon
Keng led a delegation

4
00:00:12,866 --> 00:00:17,031
of Chinese community leaders
from Singapore and Malaya to

5
00:00:17,111 --> 00:00:21,722
present a cheque for $50 million
to General Tomoyuki Yamashita,

6
00:00:21,802 --> 00:00:25,675
the commander of the army
that had taken the island.

7
00:00:25,675 --> 00:00:28,944
The next day the Syonan
Times reported it as a

8
00:00:29,024 --> 00:00:33,531
"voluntary gift" from the Chinese,
made to mark "their loyalty,

9
00:00:33,611 --> 00:00:35,650
sincerity and co-operation."

10
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:38,467
The money had in fact
been demanded of them,

11
00:00:38,547 --> 00:00:43,208
under a levy that fell on every Chinese
household and business of means,

12
00:00:43,288 --> 00:00:46,434
and when the community
could not raise all of it,

13
00:00:46,514 --> 00:00:49,675
close to half was borrowed
from a Japanese bank.

14
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:53,566
The Chinese of Singapore and
Malaya had spent the years

15
00:00:53,646 --> 00:00:58,050
before the war raising money
for China's fight against Japan.

16
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:02,935
Relief funds led by the rubber
magnate Tan Kah Kee had collected

17
00:01:03,015 --> 00:01:07,900
donations from rich and poor
alike, and in 1939 some 3,200 young

18
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:13,408
volunteers from the region had gone
to drive lorries on the Burma Road,

19
00:01:13,488 --> 00:01:17,600
as told in an earlier post
on the Nanyang volunteers.

20
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:21,512
When Singapore fell on
the 15th of February 1942,

21
00:01:21,592 --> 00:01:26,725
the Japanese military treated
the Chinese community as hostile.

22
00:01:26,725 --> 00:01:29,333
In the Sook Ching screening that followed,

23
00:01:29,413 --> 00:01:33,700
Chinese men were rounded up and
many thousands of them were killed.

24
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:37,299
In the middle of this, a
Japanese civilian official,

25
00:01:37,379 --> 00:01:39,845
Mamoru Shinozaki, brought together a

26
00:01:39,925 --> 00:01:43,250
group of Chinese leaders
who had stayed behind.

27
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:48,605
On the 2nd of March 1942 they formed
the Oversea Chinese Association

28
00:01:48,685 --> 00:01:53,400
at the Chinese Chamber of
Commerce building on Hill Street.

29
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,724
Lim Boon Keng, a doctor, reformer
and the former president of

30
00:01:57,804 --> 00:02:02,705
Amoy University in China, was made
its chairman, with the businessman

31
00:02:02,785 --> 00:02:06,900
S. Q. Wong as vice-chairman
and Shinozaki as its adviser.

32
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:10,084
The association was
presented as a body that

33
00:02:10,164 --> 00:02:13,725
would speak for the
community to its new rulers.

34
00:02:13,725 --> 00:02:17,850
Its first large task was
to raise money for them.

35
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:21,463
The military administration
called on the Chinese

36
00:02:21,543 --> 00:02:25,232
to give $50 million,
presented as an atonement for

37
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:29,226
their support of China, with
$10 million to come from

38
00:02:29,306 --> 00:02:33,075
Singapore and $40 million
from the rest of Malaya.

39
00:02:33,075 --> 00:02:36,659
The deadline was first
set for the 20th of April,

40
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:41,375
then moved to the 20th of May
and finally to the 25th of June.

41
00:02:41,375 --> 00:02:45,158
To share out the burden,
the association set a levy

42
00:02:45,238 --> 00:02:49,172
of 8 per cent on the property
of every Chinese person

43
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,353
whose property was worth more than $3,000,

44
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:56,675
and 5 per cent on the assets
of Chinese-owned companies.

45
00:02:56,675 --> 00:03:01,158
Lim Boon Keng himself,
according to an article in the

46
00:03:01,238 --> 00:03:06,575
National Library's BiblioAsia
journal, was assessed at $2,200.

47
00:03:06,575 --> 00:03:11,635
A Malaya-wide body, the Malayan
Overseas Chinese General Association,

48
00:03:11,715 --> 00:03:13,795
was set up on the 6th of June

49
00:03:13,875 --> 00:03:17,600
to coordinate the collection
across the peninsula.

50
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:21,136
Collecting the levy in a
country that had just been

51
00:03:21,216 --> 00:03:25,400
invaded proved hard, which is
why the deadline kept moving.

52
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:30,049
By the 20th of June, five days
before the final deadline,

53
00:03:30,129 --> 00:03:32,950
about $28 million had been raised.

54
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:37,278
Two days later, on the 23rd of
June, a notice in the Syonan

55
00:03:37,358 --> 00:03:41,088
Times told contributors
they could still pay at the

56
00:03:41,168 --> 00:03:45,725
Oversea-Chinese Banking Corporation
or the Sze Hai Tong Bank.

57
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:48,192
To make up the remaining $22 million,

58
00:03:48,272 --> 00:03:52,185
the association borrowed it
from the Yokohama Specie Bank,

59
00:03:52,265 --> 00:03:57,003
Japan's main foreign-exchange bank,
which had reopened in Singapore in

60
00:03:57,083 --> 00:04:01,065
March in the building of the
interned Hongkong and Shanghai

61
00:04:01,145 --> 00:04:05,000
Bank (see the earlier post
on the Yokohama Specie Bank).

62
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,747
According to BiblioAsia,
it was a secured loan at

63
00:04:08,827 --> 00:04:12,575
6 per cent interest, to
be repaid within a year.

64
00:04:12,575 --> 00:04:16,337
In effect, the Chinese community
paid part of the "gift"

65
00:04:16,417 --> 00:04:21,002
to the Japanese government with
money lent to it by a Japanese bank,

66
00:04:21,082 --> 00:04:24,375
and then owed that bank
the money with interest.

67
00:04:24,375 --> 00:04:28,400
The cheque was handed
over on the 25th of June.

68
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:32,687
The Syonan Times of the next
day carried the story on page 2

69
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:36,253
under the headline "$50
Million Gift By Chinese",

70
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:41,500
with a photograph of Yamashita
receiving the cheque from Lim Boon Keng.

71
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:45,575
The report described the
money as a voluntary gift.

72
00:04:45,575 --> 00:04:50,425
It said nothing of the levy, the
extended deadlines or the loan.

73
00:04:50,425 --> 00:04:54,311
To give a sense of scale,
the National Library Board's

74
00:04:54,391 --> 00:04:58,498
account of the Oversea Chinese
Association notes that all

75
00:04:58,578 --> 00:05:02,171
the currency in circulation
in Malaya at the time,

76
00:05:02,251 --> 00:05:07,025
including the reserves held by
banks, came to about $220 million.

77
00:05:07,025 --> 00:05:12,275
The sum demanded from one community
was close to a quarter of that.

78
00:05:12,275 --> 00:05:15,558
At the same time, the
Japanese authorities were

79
00:05:15,638 --> 00:05:19,207
bringing in their own
currency for occupied Malaya,

80
00:05:19,287 --> 00:05:22,650
issued at first at par
with the Straits dollar.

81
00:05:22,650 --> 00:05:26,376
Over the next three years
the military administration

82
00:05:26,456 --> 00:05:29,751
printed so much of it
that its value collapsed,

83
00:05:29,831 --> 00:05:32,775
as described in the post on banana money.

84
00:05:32,775 --> 00:05:37,200
In the middle of 1942 that
collapse still lay ahead,

85
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:41,525
so the $50 million was a
heavy sum in real terms.

86
00:05:41,525 --> 00:05:45,717
What became of the $22
million loan is not recorded

87
00:05:45,797 --> 00:05:49,650
in any of the sources
consulted for this post.

88
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:53,189
The Yokohama Specie Bank itself was closed

89
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:57,412
after Japan's surrender
in 1945, and its business

90
00:05:57,492 --> 00:06:01,025
passed to a successor, the Bank of Tokyo.

91
00:06:01,025 --> 00:06:03,993
The men who led the association lived with

92
00:06:04,073 --> 00:06:06,975
the episode for the rest of their lives.

93
00:06:06,975 --> 00:06:10,700
After the war, some in the
community saw the association

94
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:13,010
as having worked for the Japanese,

95
00:06:13,090 --> 00:06:17,291
while others regarded its leaders
as hostages who had done what

96
00:06:17,371 --> 00:06:20,700
they could to protect the
community under threat.

97
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:23,975
Lim Boon Keng, who had
been one of the best-known

98
00:06:24,055 --> 00:06:27,466
Chinese public figures in
Singapore before the war,

99
00:06:27,546 --> 00:06:31,175
was said to have drunk
heavily during the Occupation.

100
00:06:31,175 --> 00:06:34,613
He lived quietly after 1945 and

101
00:06:34,693 --> 00:06:38,325
died on the 1st of January 1957.

102
00:06:38,325 --> 00:06:41,658
The association's
secretary, Tan Yeok Seong,

103
00:06:41,738 --> 00:06:45,769
published his own account
of how the money was raised

104
00:06:45,849 --> 00:06:49,650
in the Journal of the
South Seas Society in 1946.

105
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:53,758
Shinozaki was a witness
at the war crimes trials

106
00:06:53,838 --> 00:06:58,025
in Singapore and was sent
back to Japan in 1948.

107
00:06:58,025 --> 00:07:02,947
In his memoir, published in English
in 1975 as "Syonan—My Story",

108
00:07:03,027 --> 00:07:07,718
he wrote that the association
and the safety passes he issued,

109
00:07:07,798 --> 00:07:12,800
which became known as "Good
Citizen's Tickets", saved many lives.

110
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:16,560
Historians have generally
read the memoir with caution,

111
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:20,550
since it presents its author
in a very favourable light.

112
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:24,500
Two decades later, the
same figure appeared again.

113
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:28,178
After mass graves of
Occupation victims were found

114
00:07:28,258 --> 00:07:31,711
around Singapore in 1962,
the community pressed

115
00:07:31,791 --> 00:07:35,625
Japan to pay what came to
be called a "blood debt".

116
00:07:35,625 --> 00:07:40,473
On the 25th of October 1966,
the governments of Singapore and

117
00:07:40,553 --> 00:07:45,644
Japan agreed on a settlement of
$50 million, half as a grant and

118
00:07:45,724 --> 00:07:50,975
half as a loan, as told in the
post on the Civilian War Memorial.

119
00:07:50,975 --> 00:07:55,391
The memorial on Beach Road,
unveiled in February 1967,

120
00:07:55,470 --> 00:07:59,300
holds the remains recovered
from those graves.

121
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:01,810
The two sums were alike in size but

122
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:04,775
were arrived at in very different ways.

123
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:08,785
The first was set by an
occupying army, collected from a

124
00:08:08,865 --> 00:08:13,175
community under threat and
partly paid with borrowed money.

125
00:08:13,175 --> 00:08:15,859
The second was negotiated and agreed

126
00:08:15,939 --> 00:08:18,550
between two sovereign governments.

127
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:22,576
Why it matters today: The $50
million "gift" is remembered far

128
00:08:22,656 --> 00:08:26,946
less than the Sook Ching that came
before it, yet it shows how the

129
00:08:27,026 --> 00:08:31,118
Occupation reached into almost
every Chinese household of means

130
00:08:31,198 --> 00:08:35,025
in Singapore and Malaya, and
how a demand made under threat

131
00:08:35,105 --> 00:08:39,475
could be recorded in the newspapers
of the day as a voluntary act.
